<code>assert this.size() == c.size() && (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.contains(c.toArray()[i]));</code>

This ensures that the list has the same number of elements as the collection and that every element in the collection is contained in the list. However, this doesn't guarantee the order. Since the problem specifies that the elements are added in the order they are returned by the collection's iterator, we should also ensure the order:

<code>assert this.size() == c.size() && (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]));</code>

Given the available methods and the need to ensure both size and order, the most appropriate assert statement is:

<code>assert this.size() == c.size() && (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]));</code>

